nesis row followed by one row after every actual B record. Do not trim helper events, publication, pending records or charged bookkeeping. No actual prefix length disclosed.\"\n  },\n  \"interval\": {\n    \"keys\": [\n      \"A_record_index\",\n      \"A_rule_line\",\n      \"first_B_record\",\n      \"B_records_exclusive\",\n      \"helper_rule_ids\",\n      \"legacy_rule_id\"\n    ],\n    \"A_record_index\": \"Zero-based ordinal in actual translated A StepRecord sequence.\",\n    \"A_rule_line\": \"Standalone normative models/sherlock/k/main.k source rule START line for the actual mapped A event, not Rust line or B ordinal.\",\n    \"first_B_record\": \"Zero-based first actual B record ordinal in interval, inclusive.\",\n    \"B_records_exclusive\": \"Zero-based exclusive actual B record end ordinal, including its separate completion/publication.\",\n    \"helper_rule_ids\": \"Exact ordered preceding charged helper interval rule IDs. Includes charged Bookkeeping if selected; excludes legacy completion/publication. The field name does not authorize omission based on event kind.\",\n    \"legacy_rule_id\": \"Normative dotted ID of separate completion. In the free-publication interval this field contains the administrative publication ID.\"\n  },\n  \"numericConvention\": \"Exact unsigned JSON integer number tokens; no floating-point casts or decimal strings. Initial absent association/rule use JSON null.\",\n  \"ruleIds\": {\n    \"convention\": \"Normative dotted IDs, not RuleIdC Debug strings. Public declaration map below covers the entire normative source inventory, NOT selected expected membership. It reveals no actual or expected schedule.\",\n    \"publicDeclarationMapping\": {\n      \"KMachineEvalLiteralValid\": \"k.machine.eval.literal.valid\",\n      \"KMachineEvalLiteralInvalid\": \"k.machine.eval.literal.invalid\",\n      \"KMachineEvalVariablePresent\": \"k.machine.eval.variable.present\",\n      \"KMachineEvalVariableAbsent\": \"k.machine.eval.variabl